DTEND:20260518T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260518T000000Z
SUMMARY:Business Foundations & Operational Strategy
DESCRIPTION:Is your business generating revenue but struggling with 
 consistency\, capacity\, or growth? In today’s 2026 environment\, small 
 business owners must build strong operational foundations that support 
 scalability\, automation\, and sustainability. This session focuses on 
 helping entrepreneurs transition from working in the business to building 
 systems that allow the business to run efficiently and grow 
 strategically.\n\nParticipants will learn how to strengthen core operations 
 including workflows\, service delivery\, pricing structure\, capacity 
 planning\, and operational roles. The session will also cover how to 
 leverage automation\, AI tools\, CRM systems\, and integrations to reduce 
 manual tasks\, improve customer experience\, and increase productivity 
 without adding staff.\n\nThis training is designed for small business 
 owners who want to improve operational efficiency\, increase 
 profitability\, prepare for growth opportunities\, and build a business 
 that can scale. By the end of the session\, participants will identify 
 operational gaps\, implement foundational systems\, and develop a practical 
 operational strategy that supports long-term business 
 sustainability.\n\nThis workshop is hosted by La-Tasha Best-Gaddy\, founder 
 and chief strategist of Infinity Bridges Inc. As a strategic visionary\, 
 La-Tasha is dedicated to creating infrastructure that generates legacy\, 
 not just income. She has spent decades building systems for small 
 businesses\, municipalities\, nonprofits\, and financial institutions\, 
 bridging technical expertise with practical strategy to elevate communities 
 often underestimated or excluded.
LOCATION:Conference Room #3214\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Austin Daniels":MAILTO:ausdaniels@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Business, Career Development, Finance
UID:LibCal-14288-16705878
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16705878
END:VEVENT
