DTEND:20260520T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260520T000000Z
SUMMARY:Testers & Tasters Cookbook Club
DESCRIPTION:\n\nTesters & Tasters Cookbook Club is a place to talk about 
 food and cooking!\n\nCome share your experiments\, experiences\, triumphs\, 
 and tragedies.\n\nThis month's theme is Fictional Recipes! But have no 
 fear: the recipes we test and taste will be 100% real\, but they must come 
 from or be inspired by a work of fiction.\n\nAt the North Regional 
 Information Desk there will be some cookbooks (these should stay in the 
 library\; if you find a recipe you like\, you may take a photo of it or ask 
 the desk staff to make you a copy) as well as individual fiction books that 
 contain recipes (feel free to take one of these and check it out). You can 
 also follow the links below or search on your own. \n\nHere are a few to 
 get you started. \n\nAnd here are some recipes from the Arsenic and Adobo 
 series by Mia Manansala.\n\nWhen you know the name of the dish you'll be 
 bringing\, please email the name and source to etobias@dconc.gov.\n\nAnd 
 don't forget some containers for leftovers!\n\nQuestions? Email 
 etobias@dconc.gov or call 919-560-0140.\n\nRegistration closes 24 hours 
 before the meeting\, but email me if you've missed the deadline and still 
 want to come.\n\nHappy Cooking to all!\n\n\n\nAll in-person programming is 
 subject to change or cancellation based on current COVID conditions.\n\n
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Emily Tobias":MAILTO:etobias@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club, Food & Cooking
UID:LibCal-14288-15946879
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15946879
END:VEVENT
